thways combine to form the new white pigment. If neither of the genes are dominant, then there is no pigment change and the blue precursor pigment remains. <br/> <br/><p>The diagram and description above explain the interaction of two genes. <b>Determine the dihybird cross phenotypic ratio.</b></p>
